WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:09.407 --> 00:00:11.909
{\an8}<i>The potion that cures all diseases?</i>

2
00:00:18.916 --> 00:00:20.668
<i>With this potion.</i>

3
00:00:20.751 --> 00:00:23.379
<i>perhaps it could cure
my mother's Eternal Slumber.</i>

4
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.842
<i>Creating Elixir of Life
requires three items.</i>

5
00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.261
<i>I don't have any of them yet.</i>

6
00:00:30.761 --> 00:00:32.763
<i>but I know where to find them.</i>

7
00:00:33.848 --> 00:00:34.724
<i>However...</i>

8
00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:38.227
<i>With my current strength. entering
that gate would be committing suicide.</i>

9
00:00:39.103 --> 00:00:40.688
<i>I must level up even higher.</i>

10
00:00:42.314 --> 00:00:43.149
I must...

11
00:00:44.692 --> 00:00:46.193
become stronger.

12
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

13
00:02:17.743 --> 00:02:20.204
Eh. you decided to accept it?

14
00:02:20.287 --> 00:02:22.206
The situation is different now.

15
00:02:22.289 --> 00:02:25.876
For your proposal
for 19 C-rank raid missions. I'm in.

16
00:02:27.002 --> 00:02:27.837
That's great.

17
00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.672
But I have one condition.

18
00:02:29.755 --> 00:02:32.007
Just say it.

19
00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:34.969
Just you and me.

20
00:02:35.052 --> 00:02:36.303
The two of us.

21
00:02:38.848 --> 00:02:43.143
Just the two of us
to conquer C-rank dungeons?

22
00:02:44.103 --> 00:02:45.062
That's right.

23
00:02:46.814 --> 00:02:49.483
But... To enter the C-rank gate.

24
00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:52.152
we need at least eight people. don't we?

25
00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.030
Just find people to make up the numbers.

26
00:02:55.614 --> 00:02:58.075
like what Hwang Dongsuk did.

27
00:03:00.327 --> 00:03:01.996
But...

28
00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:03.455
Will it be dangerous?

29
00:03:04.039 --> 00:03:05.499
It depends on how you see it.

30
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.626
As long as the two of us are safe.

31
00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.880
we can complete the 19 raid missions
without anyone getting hurt.

32
00:03:11.547 --> 00:03:14.508
{\an8}A team unscathed
in 19 consecutive missions.

33
00:03:15.342 --> 00:03:19.138
Isn't that a perfect way
to make your father acknowledge you?

34
00:03:19.972 --> 00:03:20.890
I see.

35
00:03:25.269 --> 00:03:26.812
Let's do it. Jinwoo.

36
00:03:26.896 --> 00:03:29.732
I'll take care
of team members and the gate.

37
00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:09.647
Come out.

38
00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:10.940
What do you want?

39
00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:13.484
Truly surprising.

40
00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.945
No wonder you're an S-rank hunter.

41
00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:19.323
I couldn't find the right moment
to speak to you.

42
00:04:20.032 --> 00:04:21.825
Sorry for disturbing you
during your training.

43
00:04:21.909 --> 00:04:24.036
Here is my business card.

44
00:04:34.088 --> 00:04:37.341
It's been over a decade
since the gates appeared.

45
00:04:37.424 --> 00:04:39.969
The world has changed drastically.

46
00:04:41.011 --> 00:04:45.349
Now infrastructure. economy.
media. and even politics

47
00:04:45.432 --> 00:04:48.435
are all inextricably linked
to the dungeon.

48
00:04:49.436 --> 00:04:52.815
Especially the infrastructure
that is vital to the common people.

49
00:04:52.898 --> 00:04:56.277
Without resources from the dungeon.
it'd be hard to sustain operations.

50
00:04:56.777 --> 00:05:01.824
And the only ones who can bring
such valuable resources back

51
00:05:01.907 --> 00:05:03.325
are the hunters.

52
00:05:04.326 --> 00:05:06.954
And the one managing these hunters

53
00:05:07.579 --> 00:05:10.749
{\an8}is the government agency
known as Hunter's Association.

54
00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:16.380
<i>The Hunter's Association
will classify awakened hunters.</i>

55
00:05:16.463 --> 00:05:18.799
<i>register and manage them accordingly.</i>

56
00:05:19.633 --> 00:05:22.261
<i>They assign manpower
to deal with unwanted gates</i>

57
00:05:22.344 --> 00:05:24.847
<i>and also bear the heavy
responsibility in Dungeon Breaks.</i>

58
00:05:25.681 --> 00:05:29.685
But in the end. the association
is just a government agency.

59
00:05:29.768 --> 00:05:32.980
These resources are enough
to sustain operations.

60
00:05:33.063 --> 00:05:35.733
but those who control
most of resources are guilds.

61
00:05:35.816 --> 00:05:38.986
the corporations
that center around hunters.

62
00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:42.906
The guilds obtain massive profits
from the resources

63
00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.700
acquired from the dungeons.

64
00:05:45.451 --> 00:05:48.704
<i>Among them. Hunters Guild.
White Tiger Guild.</i>

65
00:05:48.787 --> 00:05:52.458
<i>Feind Guild. Fame Guild. and Knights Guild</i>

66
00:05:52.541 --> 00:05:54.710
<i>are the five major guilds in the country.</i>

67
00:05:55.836 --> 00:05:59.048
<i>These guilds have almost
monopolized all the resources.</i>

68
00:06:00.758 --> 00:06:04.428
I cannot just sit here and watch.

69
00:06:05.012 --> 00:06:08.432
Not to mention letting
these resources vital to the people

70
00:06:08.515 --> 00:06:11.852
fall into the hands of those brutes.

71
00:06:12.936 --> 00:06:15.939
It should be us. who have supported
the nation's development.

72
00:06:16.023 --> 00:06:18.067
to take on the responsibility
to manage them.

73
00:06:20.027 --> 00:06:21.528
For this purpose.

74
00:06:21.612 --> 00:06:23.864
we must establish a guild.

75
00:06:25.032 --> 00:06:26.200
Yes.

76
00:06:29.161 --> 00:06:30.412
<i>That being said.</i>

77
00:06:30.913 --> 00:06:34.708
<i>as my brother and I jointly run a guild
and headhunt S-rank hunters.</i>

78
00:06:34.792 --> 00:06:36.293
<i>the risks are too great.</i>

79
00:06:36.376 --> 00:06:37.211
<i>But.</i>

80
00:06:37.878 --> 00:06:39.088
<i>my current self...</i>

81
00:06:54.561 --> 00:06:57.564
<i>It stopped counting the quests
that exceeded the goal?</i>

82
00:06:58.524 --> 00:07:03.695
<i>Does it mean I can't get the reward
for the previous secret quest.</i>

83
00:07:03.779 --> 00:07:06.365
<i>Cursed Random Loot Box?</i>

84
00:07:07.116 --> 00:07:11.453
<i>I thought I could get another item
like The Demon Castle's Key.</i>

85
00:07:12.162 --> 00:07:12.996
<i>No.</i>

86
00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:15.499
<i>Even if it's a regular random box.</i>

87
00:07:15.582 --> 00:07:19.878
<i>it's possible to get something
like an instance dungeon's key.</i>

88
00:07:27.886 --> 00:07:29.304
<i>Makes sense.</i>

89
00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:38.230
{\an8}<i>At this level. three ability points
are no longer enough.</i>

90
00:07:39.064 --> 00:07:41.650
<i>I really want to level up quickly.</i>

91
00:07:41.733 --> 00:07:44.695
<i>but now I can only wait
for Jinho's C-rank dungeon missions.</i>

92
00:07:46.613 --> 00:07:47.781
<i>That's right.</i>

93
00:07:47.865 --> 00:07:48.991
<i>Penalty Zone.</i>

94
00:07:49.074 --> 00:07:50.784
<i>As long as I kill those centipedes there...</i>

95
00:07:51.577 --> 00:07:52.494
<i>No.</i>

96
00:07:52.578 --> 00:07:55.205
<i>Now I might escape
more easily than before.</i>

97
00:07:55.289 --> 00:07:56.331
<i>But to defeat it...</i>

98
00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.418
<i>Besides. I might not be able
to gain any points.</i>

99
00:08:03.005 --> 00:08:05.466
<i>D-rank gate mission?</i>

100
00:08:05.966 --> 00:08:08.927
<i>It's a request from the
Hunter's Association for making up a team.</i>

101
00:08:09.595 --> 00:08:12.556
<i>which means I can't fight alone.</i>

102
00:08:13.056 --> 00:08:14.057
<i>Should I refuse?</i>

103
00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.479
<i>Well. it's better than nothing.</i>

104
00:08:23.192 --> 00:08:24.610
<i>I have no time to waste.</i>

105
00:08:35.746 --> 00:08:37.623
I still can't defeat you. master.

106
00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.127
It won't be so easy for you to defeat me.

107
00:08:42.753 --> 00:08:44.671
However. it's still a pity.

108
00:08:45.214 --> 00:08:47.508
I really want to spar with you
in your top condition.

109
00:08:47.591 --> 00:08:48.884
You're bringing this up again.

110
00:08:49.426 --> 00:08:51.553
It's been several months.

111
00:08:55.057 --> 00:08:56.725
An urgent call-up?

112
00:08:57.392 --> 00:09:00.437
Low-rank hunters are
just fated to run errands.

113
00:09:01.021 --> 00:09:03.649
Master. have you never
thought about retiring?

114
00:09:03.732 --> 00:09:04.816
Retiring?

115
00:09:09.947 --> 00:09:11.114
Indeed.

116
00:09:11.198 --> 00:09:15.160
An old man with only one arm
might only be a hindrance.

117
00:09:15.244 --> 00:09:17.162
No. that's not what I meant...

118
00:09:17.246 --> 00:09:20.582
I lost an arm. yet I survived.

119
00:09:21.124 --> 00:09:23.085
I don't have much time left.

120
00:09:23.669 --> 00:09:26.755
At least before I die.
I hope to do more for this world.

121
00:09:35.556 --> 00:09:37.099
I got a new raid mission.

122
00:09:38.642 --> 00:09:39.977
Dear.

123
00:09:40.811 --> 00:09:43.689
Isn't it about time
you give up being a hunter?

124
00:09:44.231 --> 00:09:45.691
You bring it up again?

125
00:09:46.191 --> 00:09:47.818
Because it's too dangerous.

126
00:09:47.901 --> 00:09:50.112
So many people died in the last mission.

127
00:09:50.654 --> 00:09:53.490
You almost didn't make it out. right?

128
00:09:54.324 --> 00:09:56.201
Hmm... Yeah.

129
00:09:57.286 --> 00:09:58.829
Daddy. hug.

130
00:10:01.248 --> 00:10:04.084
But. next year.
Eunji will be going to kindergarten.

131
00:10:04.167 --> 00:10:05.669
and Eunha is also going to junior high.

132
00:10:05.752 --> 00:10:07.254
We need money. don't we?

133
00:10:07.337 --> 00:10:08.630
That's true.

134
00:10:08.714 --> 00:10:10.340
It's okay.

135
00:10:10.424 --> 00:10:14.595
The association wouldn't send us low-rank
hunters to overly dangerous dungeons.

136
00:10:15.887 --> 00:10:18.140
Last time was just an exception.

137
00:10:18.932 --> 00:10:20.142
Yes.

138
00:10:20.225 --> 00:10:22.352
Sorry. I shouldn't have said that.

139
00:10:22.436 --> 00:10:23.645
Don't mind it.

140
00:10:24.438 --> 00:10:25.856
Be careful. okay?

141
00:10:26.523 --> 00:10:27.524
Okay.

142
00:10:27.608 --> 00:10:28.442
I love you.

143
00:10:28.942 --> 00:10:29.776
Daddy.

144
00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:31.194
Oh. what is it?

145
00:10:31.737 --> 00:10:33.947
Daddy. are you very powerful?

146
00:10:34.031 --> 00:10:35.741
Of course.

147
00:10:35.824 --> 00:10:38.994
I can defeat scary monsters.

148
00:10:39.077 --> 00:10:40.412
That's amazing.

149
00:10:40.495 --> 00:10:42.956
Daddy. you really are the best.

150
00:10:44.374 --> 00:10:46.209
You tricked me.

151
00:10:49.171 --> 00:10:50.589
{\an8}What are you referring to?

152
00:10:51.089 --> 00:10:54.593
You pushed the bothersome
media interview onto me.

153
00:10:54.676 --> 00:10:55.761
I saw it on TV.

154
00:10:55.844 --> 00:10:58.013
You did super well.

155
00:10:58.096 --> 00:11:00.515
Your speech really hit home.

156
00:11:00.599 --> 00:11:02.476
Stop saying that.

157
00:11:02.559 --> 00:11:06.188
That was originally your job. right?

158
00:11:06.271 --> 00:11:08.815
But Chairman Go requested

159
00:11:08.899 --> 00:11:14.780
to show the public the work attitude
and honest character of strong hunters.

160
00:11:15.322 --> 00:11:18.158
I don't think
I'm quite suited for this task.

161
00:11:18.909 --> 00:11:21.119
So you know you're not honest.

162
00:11:22.871 --> 00:11:23.914
Forget it.

163
00:11:23.997 --> 00:11:25.665
All right. what do you want from me?

164
00:11:26.166 --> 00:11:30.587
You didn't summon me
just to hear me complain. right?

165
00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:35.509
I must inform you of a recent event.

166
00:11:36.468 --> 00:11:39.846
Yoojin Construction
seems to want to establish a guild.

167
00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:42.891
I know that. They are looking
for people under the table.

168
00:11:43.475 --> 00:11:45.644
I've also heard
they are poaching my people.

169
00:11:46.186 --> 00:11:50.565
Since you have known it.
it seems I am meddling unnecessarily.

170
00:11:50.649 --> 00:11:54.194
You knew all along that I would know.

171
00:11:54.277 --> 00:11:55.654
Stop beating around the bush.

172
00:11:57.406 --> 00:11:58.615
I'll ask you again.

173
00:11:59.533 --> 00:12:00.951
What do you want from me?

174
00:12:04.704 --> 00:12:07.332
<i>You haven't been calling recently.</i>

175
00:12:07.416 --> 00:12:09.000
<i>Is everything going well?</i>

176
00:12:09.876 --> 00:12:11.920
-Hmm.
<i>-How's your work?</i>

177
00:12:12.754 --> 00:12:13.880
Hmm.

178
00:12:13.964 --> 00:12:15.048
It's okay.

179
00:12:15.132 --> 00:12:18.051
<i>You have always been timid.</i>

180
00:12:18.135 --> 00:12:20.554
<i>Doesn't working as a Hunter
make you uncomfortable?</i>

181
00:12:21.096 --> 00:12:22.305
I heard you're a B-rank hunter.

182
00:12:22.806 --> 00:12:25.600
<i>If it were someone else.
they would probably be strong.</i>

183
00:12:25.684 --> 00:12:28.562
<i>But you'd probably be a burden to others.</i>

184
00:12:29.062 --> 00:12:31.356
<i>You'd better come back
and help out at home.</i>

185
00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:32.566
<i>Your dad is also worried about you...</i>

186
00:12:32.649 --> 00:12:34.568
Don't make decisions for me. okay?

187
00:12:35.527 --> 00:12:37.988
{\an8}I'll make my own decisions.
I don't need you to interfere.

188
00:12:38.071 --> 00:12:39.573
<i>Wait. why are you...</i>

189
00:12:46.997 --> 00:12:48.540
A burden to others?

190
00:12:50.667 --> 00:12:51.501
But.

191
00:12:55.297 --> 00:12:58.341
I'll just give it another go.

192
00:13:30.332 --> 00:13:31.291
Excuse me.

193
00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:36.087
What is it. Hunter Cha Hae-In?

194
00:13:36.671 --> 00:13:40.842
Someone from Yoojin Construction
tried to poach me during my training.

195
00:13:41.426 --> 00:13:42.552
I came to report to you.

196
00:13:43.595 --> 00:13:44.513
I see.

197
00:13:44.596 --> 00:13:47.682
{\an8}<i>It seems they want
to establish a new guild</i>

198
00:13:47.766 --> 00:13:50.936
<i>and want me to be the guild master.</i>

199
00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:53.313
You've come to report to me.

200
00:13:53.396 --> 00:13:56.942
Can I take it as
you've declined their offer?

201
00:13:57.025 --> 00:13:59.402
Yes. I declined right on the spot.

202
00:14:00.278 --> 00:14:01.613
I'm relieved.

203
00:14:01.696 --> 00:14:03.073
Thank you very much.

204
00:14:03.156 --> 00:14:04.157
It's nothing.

205
00:14:04.241 --> 00:14:05.408
By the way.

206
00:14:05.492 --> 00:14:09.162
I saw Mr. Baek on my way here.

207
00:14:09.746 --> 00:14:11.456
What did he come to talk to you about?

208
00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:24.261
What are your thoughts on Jeju Island?

209
00:14:25.053 --> 00:14:26.346
Jeju Island?

210
00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:28.473
Why do you ask that?

211
00:14:29.057 --> 00:14:32.936
After the third raid mission.
the island was ordered off-limits.

212
00:14:33.562 --> 00:14:36.356
Now. there are only periodic
patrols along the coast.

213
00:14:36.898 --> 00:14:40.443
And the public is informed that
a memorial service is held there annually.

214
00:14:41.111 --> 00:14:45.365
People have forgotten the island
along with the fear.

215
00:14:45.907 --> 00:14:48.368
But that's unavoidable. isn't it?

216
00:14:48.451 --> 00:14:49.744
However.

217
00:14:49.828 --> 00:14:53.373
whether the gates
have become part of daily life.

218
00:14:53.456 --> 00:14:56.418
or I'm hailed
as the ultimate weapon of mankind.

219
00:14:56.501 --> 00:15:00.463
I will not forget that island.
nor what happened there.

220
00:15:01.464 --> 00:15:03.383
In the near future.

221
00:15:03.466 --> 00:15:05.719
I will definitely conquer
that island again.

222
00:15:06.553 --> 00:15:07.596
For that reason.

223
00:15:07.679 --> 00:15:10.265
we cannot afford to be divided now.

224
00:15:10.849 --> 00:15:13.476
We must unite. increase our numbers.

225
00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:15.812
and sway public opinion.

226
00:15:16.396 --> 00:15:19.232
That's what those interviews
and nurturing of newcomers are for?

227
00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:28.825
Aren't you the same?

228
00:15:30.118 --> 00:15:32.537
<i>You have also left something behind
on that island.</i>

229
00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:40.837
Eunseok.

230
00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:42.839
Byung-gu.

231
00:15:47.552 --> 00:15:48.386
Please.

232
00:15:49.137 --> 00:15:50.180
Help me...

233
00:15:52.223 --> 00:15:53.600
kill them.

234
00:15:56.686 --> 00:15:57.562
I'm going out.

235
00:15:58.188 --> 00:15:59.898
Still working on the holiday?

236
00:16:01.566 --> 00:16:02.984
You've been doing this often lately.

237
00:16:04.611 --> 00:16:05.528
Yes.

238
00:16:05.612 --> 00:16:10.158
You used to get hurt
every time you went through the gate.

239
00:16:10.742 --> 00:16:11.952
Is this the result of exercise?

240
00:16:12.452 --> 00:16:13.370
Perhaps.

241
00:16:13.954 --> 00:16:18.124
{\an8}Anyway. I can earn money steadily now.
Isn't that a good thing?

242
00:16:18.625 --> 00:16:20.043
It is...

243
00:16:20.627 --> 00:16:22.587
Eh. brother? Don't you need luggage?

244
00:16:23.213 --> 00:16:25.298
No need. I'm heading out.

245
00:16:25.382 --> 00:16:26.675
Eh. wait.

246
00:16:30.053 --> 00:16:32.222
It's not like going
to the convenience store.

247
00:16:35.892 --> 00:16:39.312
<i>My awakening is not
a physical type of awakening.</i>

248
00:16:39.396 --> 00:16:41.356
<i>My swordsmanship
can't harm the magic beasts.</i>

249
00:16:41.982 --> 00:16:43.733
<i>The swordsmanship
that I've practiced for decades</i>

250
00:16:43.817 --> 00:16:46.069
<i>turns out to be useless in the dungeon.</i>

251
00:16:46.653 --> 00:16:51.074
{\an8}<i>The fact that I. a swordsman. awakened
as a Mage is also a twist of fate.</i>

252
00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:53.994
{\an8}<i>Could there be some reason behind it?</i>

253
00:16:57.747 --> 00:16:58.581
You are...

254
00:16:59.249 --> 00:17:00.208
Mr. Song.

255
00:17:00.709 --> 00:17:02.377
I was wondering if I was mistaken.

256
00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.753
Are you Sung?

257
00:17:04.379 --> 00:17:05.380
Long time no see.

258
00:17:05.964 --> 00:17:08.216
I never thought that
I would see you here again.

259
00:17:08.299 --> 00:17:10.051
That being said.

260
00:17:10.135 --> 00:17:12.804
where is that immature young man?

261
00:17:12.887 --> 00:17:15.473
In just a few months.
you've changed so much.

262
00:17:16.808 --> 00:17:17.934
And...

263
00:17:18.018 --> 00:17:20.395
How come your leg is fine?

264
00:17:20.478 --> 00:17:24.357
Well... When I woke up in the hospital.
my leg was back to normal.

265
00:17:24.858 --> 00:17:26.276
I see.

266
00:17:26.359 --> 00:17:30.905
There might be a high-level healer among
the hunters who came to rescue.

267
00:17:31.823 --> 00:17:33.116
Regardless.

268
00:17:33.199 --> 00:17:35.952
it's great to see a young talent
making a recovery.

269
00:17:36.036 --> 00:17:37.537
Thank you.

270
00:17:38.163 --> 00:17:39.664
But you...

271
00:17:40.165 --> 00:17:41.624
As for me.

272
00:17:41.708 --> 00:17:44.753
I didn't get it treated soon enough.

273
00:17:44.836 --> 00:17:45.962
But it's all right.

274
00:17:46.546 --> 00:17:47.881
What's more important is.

275
00:17:47.964 --> 00:17:50.550
I heard from the association staff
that you are all right.

276
00:17:50.633 --> 00:17:52.844
but I'm glad to be able
to see you like this again.

277
00:17:52.927 --> 00:17:54.721
Mr. Song. why did you come here?

278
00:17:55.221 --> 00:17:58.391
I was summoned by the association.
I heard that it's a D-rank mission.

279
00:17:58.475 --> 00:17:59.851
You are in it too?

280
00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:15.033
I can't believe this.

281
00:18:16.159 --> 00:18:18.369
The members from that mission.

282
00:18:21.039 --> 00:18:22.290
Jinwoo.

283
00:18:22.874 --> 00:18:23.750
Joohee.

284
00:18:25.168 --> 00:18:26.461
And

285
00:18:26.544 --> 00:18:28.046
Mr. Kim and Mr. Kang.

286
00:18:29.881 --> 00:18:30.965
<i>So be it.</i>

287
00:18:31.591 --> 00:18:35.804
<i>After all. we abandoned Sung
and fled that place.</i>

288
00:18:36.638 --> 00:18:39.099
<i>Kim even drew his sword against me.</i>

289
00:18:39.182 --> 00:18:41.976
<i>I suppose he is too ashamed to face us.</i>

290
00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:43.353
<i>But...</i>

291
00:18:43.436 --> 00:18:47.190
<i>The five survivors of that tragedy
are once again together.</i>

292
00:18:47.273 --> 00:18:48.191
<i>So...</i>

293
00:18:48.775 --> 00:18:49.818
Jinwoo.

294
00:18:49.901 --> 00:18:51.236
It's you. right?

295
00:18:51.736 --> 00:18:53.363
You've changed a lot.

296
00:18:53.905 --> 00:18:55.865
Yes. It's been a long time.

297
00:18:55.949 --> 00:18:57.951
You've grown much taller.

298
00:18:58.034 --> 00:18:58.993
And your leg.

299
00:18:59.536 --> 00:19:01.704
When I came to visit. you were already...

300
00:19:01.788 --> 00:19:03.289
Visit?

301
00:19:08.503 --> 00:19:09.754
Oh.

302
00:19:09.838 --> 00:19:12.966
There's a beautiful lady here too.

303
00:19:15.218 --> 00:19:16.427
What's the matter?

304
00:19:16.511 --> 00:19:18.888
Are you with that young man?

305
00:19:19.389 --> 00:19:20.890
Why don't you come to us...

306
00:19:20.974 --> 00:19:22.350
Shut up.

307
00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:26.688
You are not here for a hike.

308
00:19:30.191 --> 00:19:33.486
Now. I will explain
to all the general hunters.

309
00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:34.571
Please come this way.

310
00:19:35.446 --> 00:19:36.531
What's going on?

311
00:19:36.614 --> 00:19:41.119
They are the substitute prisoners
who will join you on the mission today.

312
00:19:41.202 --> 00:19:42.787
Substitute prisoners?

313
00:19:42.871 --> 00:19:45.248
We have to go on a mission with criminals?

314
00:19:45.331 --> 00:19:47.292
Although they are hunters
with convictions.

315
00:19:47.375 --> 00:19:50.420
they wish to lessen their sentences.
so they will not harm you.

316
00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:54.048
There is a shortage
of manpower in this area.

317
00:19:54.132 --> 00:19:55.175
Please bear with us.

318
00:19:55.925 --> 00:19:57.552
How can this be?

319
00:19:58.178 --> 00:20:02.098
Kang Taeshik from Hunter's Association's
Surveillance Team will accompany you.

320
00:20:02.182 --> 00:20:03.683
He is a B-rank hunter.

321
00:20:03.766 --> 00:20:09.314
Even in the event of danger. he can
easily deal with three C-rank prisoners.

322
00:20:09.397 --> 00:20:10.982
So please rest assured.

323
00:20:11.566 --> 00:20:12.650
Something feels wrong.

324
00:20:13.234 --> 00:20:15.069
Joohee. you shouldn't go.

325
00:20:15.612 --> 00:20:16.696
What about you?

326
00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:18.656
I'm going.

327
00:20:22.202 --> 00:20:23.828
Then I'm going too.

328
00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:26.956
I understand.

329
00:20:27.999 --> 00:20:31.544
Ah. the taste of freedom is wonderful.

330
00:20:32.128 --> 00:20:33.713
We are not slaves.

331
00:20:33.796 --> 00:20:35.548
Do you have to treat us this way?

332
00:20:35.632 --> 00:20:36.758
Shut up.

333
00:20:36.841 --> 00:20:38.051
You are prisoners.

334
00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:42.180
If you dare to make a reckless move.
you know what will happen to you.

335
00:20:45.767 --> 00:20:49.479
I'm Kang Taeshik from the Hunter's
Association's Surveillance Team.

336
00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:53.441
I will take responsibility
for monitoring them.

337
00:20:53.524 --> 00:20:54.567
Please be assured.

338
00:20:55.693 --> 00:20:58.696
Who will be the leader
of this raid mission?

339
00:20:59.948 --> 00:21:03.409
Sung. can I be the Captain?

340
00:21:03.493 --> 00:21:04.619
Yes. of course.

341
00:21:06.663 --> 00:21:08.581
Thank you for giving me another chance.

342
00:21:08.665 --> 00:21:10.041
Mr. Song.

343
00:21:10.625 --> 00:21:13.753
That day. due to my mistake.
seven people lost their lives.

344
00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:16.756
I am to blame
for not being able to protect them.

345
00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:20.551
But. thanks to you. six people survived.

346
00:21:21.177 --> 00:21:23.721
Please allow me to thank you
on behalf of the five of them.

347
00:21:24.472 --> 00:21:26.557
{\an8}I thank you from the bottom of my heart.

348
00:21:27.267 --> 00:21:29.560
Mr. Song. Please raise your head.

349
00:21:32.272 --> 00:21:35.400
Kim. are you okay with me
being the Captain?

350
00:21:38.069 --> 00:21:39.487
Whatever.

351
00:21:46.286 --> 00:21:48.037
{\an8}That's it then.

352
00:21:48.121 --> 00:21:50.748
{\an8}I'll lead the team in the dungeon.

353
00:21:50.832 --> 00:21:52.166
Understood.

354
00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:53.251
Then let's set off.

355
00:22:01.384 --> 00:22:03.011
{\an8}So. let's go

356
00:22:04.512 --> 00:22:05.471
into the dungeon.

356
